LLVM masked.scatter with overlapping addresses is guaranteed to execute in element order from least-significant to most-significant lane. Thus, for duplicate addresses, higher-numbered active lanes overwrite lower-numbered active lanes, equivalent to serial scalar stores:

```text
for (i = 0; i < N; i++)
  if (mask[i])
    ptrs[i] = value[i];
```

This ordering must be preserved even when the scatter is split into multiple operations: the lower-element part must be chained before the higher-element part.
